    "lineStart": 0,
    "memoText": "\n \n                         VETO MESSAGE - No. 375\n \nTO THE SENATE:\n \nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bills:\n \nSenate Bill Number 7383, entitled:\n \n    \"AN ACT to legalize, validate, ratify and confirm the actions of the\n      Panama  central  school  district  notwithstanding  the failure to\n      timely file final building cost reports with the education depart-\n      ment\"\n \nSenate Bill Number 8178, entitled:\n \n    \"AN ACT relating to validating certain acts by  the  Roscoe  central\n      school  district  relating to final building cost reports required\n      to be filed with the education department\"\n \nSenate Bill Number 8730, entitled:\n \n    \"AN ACT relating to legalizing, validating, ratifying and confirming\n      a transportation contract of the Fulton city school district\"\n\nSenate Bill Number 8764-A, entitled:\n \n    \"AN ACT relating to legalizing, validating, ratifying and confirming\n      a transportation contract of the Port Washington Union Free School\n      District\"\n \nSenate Bill Number 8802, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  in  relation  to  legalizing,  validating,  ratifying  and\n      confirming  certain  transportation  contracts of the Corning city\n      school district\"\n \nTO THE ASSEMBLY:\n \nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bills:\n \nAssembly Bill Number 11174, entitled:\n \n    \"AN ACT to validate certain acts of Newburgh  Enlarged  city  school\n      district with regard to certain capital improvement projects\"\n \nAssembly Bill Number 11175, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  to  validate  certain  acts  of  Chester Union Free school\n      district with regard to certain capital improvement projects\"\n \n    NOT APPROVED\n \n  Each of these bills would authorize, outside of the State budget proc-\ness, payment of State expense-based  education  aid  above  the  amounts\ncalculated and previously agreed to under current law.\n \n  These  bills  would  forgive the return of State building aid payments\nfrom the Panama Central  School  District,  the  Roscoe  Central  School\n \nDistrict,  the  Newburgh  Enlarged City School District, and the Chester\nCentral School District, and would reverse disallowance of State  trans-\nportation  aid  payments  to  the  Fulton City School District, the Port\nWashington  Union  Free  School  District,  and  the Corning City School\nDistrict. The payments withheld or to  be  recovered  for  these  school\ndistricts  each resulted from violation of State laws that were known to\nthe districts at the time, and related  to  the  districts'  failure  to\nproperly obtain authorization for expenses reimbursable by the State.\n \n  In  both the 2017 and 2018 State Budgets, the Legislature and I agreed\nto payment provisions to mitigate outstanding filing penalties for these\nschool districts. As well, some of these school districts have  benefit-\nted from special legislation adopted in the budget to extend the payback\nperiod for their respective penalties, and others have received legisla-\ntive aid through the budget.\n \n  I have vetoed several similar bills in the past due to their financial\nimpacts  outside of the State budget process. While bills of this nature\nhave infrequently been signed due to  extenuating  circumstances,  these\npresent bills do not contain such circumstances.\n \n  These  bills  would create new financial obligations not accounted for\nwithin the State's financial plan.   Such funding  decisions  should  be\naddressed  within  the  context of the annual budget negotiations. These\nbills would also violate existing agreements that were previously  nego-\ntiated  with the Legislature during the budget negotiation process. I am\ntherefore constrained to veto these bills.\n \n  These bills are disapproved.                (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n \n                               __________\n",
